1
00:05:06,315 --> 00:05:12,315
So Many Mr. Wrongs. So Few Mr. Rights.

2
00:10:12,631 --> 00:10:18,631
Broken English is a comedy, drama, romance film directed by Zoe Cassavetes.

3
00:15:18,947 --> 00:15:24,947
Nora Wilder is freaking out.

4
00:20:25,263 --> 00:20:31,263
Everyone around her is either in a relationship, married, or has children, while she's in her
thirties, alone with job she's outgrown and a mother who constantly reminds her of it all.

5
00:25:31,578 --> 00:25:37,578
Not to mention her best friend Audrey's "perfect marriage".

6
00:30:37,894 --> 00:30:43,894
But after a series of disastrous dates, Nora unexpectedly meets Julien, a
quirky Frenchman who opens her eyes to a lot more than love.

7
00:35:44,210 --> 00:35:50,210
Nora Wilder, played by Parker Posey.

8
00:40:50,526 --> 00:40:56,526
Audrey Andrews, played by Drea De Matteo.

9
00:45:56,842 --> 00:46:02,842
Mark Andrews, played by Tim Guinee.

10
00:51:03,157 --> 00:51:09,157
Vivien Wilder-Mann, played by Gena Rowlands.

11
00:56:09,473 --> 00:56:15,473
Julien, played by Melvil Poupaud.

12
01:01:15,789 --> 01:01:21,789
Nick Gable, played by Justin Theroux.

13
01:06:22,105 --> 01:06:28,105
Broken English is a 2007 American romantic comedy-drama film written and
directed by Zoe Cassavetes, in her feature directorial debut.

14
01:11:28,421 --> 01:11:34,421
The film stars Parker Posey, Melvil Poupaud, Drea de Matteo,
Justin Theroux, Peter Bogdanovich, and Gena Rowlands.

15
01:16:34,736 --> 01:16:40,736
Broken English had its world premiere at the Sundance Film Festival on January 20, 2007
and a limited theatrical release in the United States on June 22, 2007.

16
01:21:41,052 --> 01:21:47,052
The film was nominated for two Independent Spirit Awards: Best Female
Lead for Posey and Best First Screenplay for Cassavetes.

17
01:26:47,368 --> 01:26:53,368
The film explores themes of career woman, single, woman director.

18
01:31:53,684 --> 01:31:59,684
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
